# L §6.1 (round 14): "The two sides are of one sort: ... two rows of one type, or two movements; any other pair is
# refused (LOAD-SAME)"; L §8.3 LOAD-SAME "same <p> = <q>: <what p is> and <what q is>" (a row and a movement, rows of
# types <T> and <T'>, a def, an index or another item). a.rate is a
# row, b.gift a movement: LOAD-SAME. (Writer 6's U-21.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "189c67e64082cc127bcde306ff8dec3dc2654a4a1614c037c3ed2747cd411199"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "f79aee6185a3e673324158e5fc3f586f114b6582220f963505c0ac556b8569af"
  same a.rate = b.gift
ask r: a.rate
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input income[p in persons]: money PLN
input rate: num
def twice: money PLN = income[ana] + income[ola] at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ana, ola] lives 2000-01-01..
  income[ana] = 100.00 PLN "umowa"
  income[ola] = 10.00 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  rate = 0.5 "umowa"
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input pocket[p in persons]: money PLN
input share: money PLN
input gday: date
move gift: transfers
  on gday
  leg cash from world to wsp amount share
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ben, ola_k] lives 2000-01-01..
  pocket[ben] = 50.00 PLN "umowa"
  pocket[ola_k] = 5.00 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  share = 5.00 PLN "umowa"
  gday = 2026-03-01 "umowa"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME same a.rate = b.gift: a row and a movement ...
